      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stony Plain was originally called Dog Rump Creek in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stony_Plain%2C_Alberta"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dr. James Hector, a geologist on the Palliser expedition, noted boulders that gave Stony Plain its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stony_Plain%2C_Alberta"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stony Plain is famous for its vibrant painted murals that chronicle the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.comeexplorecanada.com/alberta/stony-plain"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every June, Stony Plain celebrates Farmers' Days with a parade, rodeo, pancake breakfast, and fairgrounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stony_Plain%2C_Alberta"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In July, the town hosts the Great White North Triathlon, drawing runners from across Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stony_Plain%2C_Alberta"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Early August brings the Blueberry Bluegrass and Country Music Festival, the largest bluegrass event in western Canada.",
